# Copy to .env.local for local dev. In production the frontend is served from the same origin as the
# gateway, so this can be left empty there.
#
# RECOMMENDED for local dev: leave VITE_API_BASE empty. The Vite dev server proxies /api and /auth
# to the gateway over HTTPS (https://localhost:8443) with cert verification disabled (vite.config.ts),
# so the browser never sees the dev self-signed cert and there's no mixed-content prompt.
#
# If you instead point the browser straight at the gateway, use the HTTPS edge and accept the
# self-signed cert once: VITE_API_BASE=https://localhost:8443 (CORS allows http://localhost:5173).
VITE_API_BASE=

# ── Taste Match prototype (LOCAL, ?taste-match) — OPTIONAL Pexels enrichment ──────────────────────────
# The Taste Match game sources fresh 4-lens imagery (the fruit / its farm / its region / related nature).
# This key is OPTIONAL: leave it UNSET and the game works out of the box on a curated Wikimedia Commons
# fallback set (no API call) plus keyless Commons live-search. Set it to enable richer, more varied live
# photos from Pexels (free tier: ~200 req/hr, 20k/mo). Get a key at https://www.pexels.com/api/.
# VITE_PEXELS_KEY=
